-- #822 S0 REGRESSION PIN, CROSS-MODULE half (adversarial review of PR #1011).
--
-- The first cut of #822 stored graded kinds under the bare type-parameter NAME in
-- `universeIfaceParamKinds`, which is a GLOBAL data-universe accumulator and is NOT
-- import-scoped.  So merely compiling `gradedmod` in the same run re-kinded every
-- `g e a` in every other module of the graph — including `plainmod`, which imports
-- nothing from it — turning `e` into a row that erases to `<>`.
--
-- `held` below is the observable: with the leak it prints `held : a <> b -> a <> b`
-- (the Row slot erased); correctly scoped it prints three independent variables.
-- The gate diffs the entry's schemes, so the golden IS the discriminator.
import gradedmod.{GThenable}
import plainmod.{keep}

export held : g e a -> g e a
held x = keep x
